{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788292362,"nonce":"HVCFg5CGnrNHGd/Ioaru/SONrx4=","message":"PREMISE VERIFIED, AND THE RE-READING THAT WOULD HAVE EXONERATED THE CAP IS\nREFUTED. The round brief put it as a fork: `PawnSerializer.Rank` bands bleeding\nfirst and shipped in `c85189d` (2026-08-30), BEFORE the M1 run — so either the\ncap was not the mechanism, or something else truncated the row. Neither. **The\ncap is the mechanism and the sort that shipped is its proximate cause**, because\n\"bleeding first\" ranks the CONSEQUENCE below every WOUND that produces it.\n\n\n`transcripts/m1-20260831/` — pawn 995 was read FIVE times, not four\n(`157`, `161`, `163`, `165`, `167`):\n\n| dir | hediffs_total | hediffs_more | rows | bleed_rate | BloodLoss present |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 157-pawn | 27 | 7 | 20 | 2.40 | **no** |\n| 161-pawn | 36 | 16 | 20 | 2.97 | **no** |\n| 163-pawn | 38 | 18 | 20 | 3.35 | **no** |\n| 165-pawn | 39 | 19 | 20 | 3.48 | **no** |\n| 167-pawn | 39 | 19 | 20 | 3.46 | **no** |\n\n`167-pawn`'s twenty rows are 17 `Bite` + 3 `Scratch`, and **every one carries a\nnon-null `bleeding`** (0.20 down to 0.06) with `life_threatening:false`\nthroughout. That is twenty rank-4 rows filling a cap of 20 exactly. The sort ran\nand worked as written; there was no slot left for anything below rank 4.\n\n\n1. **`Verse/Hediff.BleedRate` is `public virtual float BleedRate =\u003e 0f`.**\n   `BloodLoss` declares no `hediffClass`, so it is not `Hediff_Injury` and does\n   not override it. Its `BleedRate` is 0 by construction — **`Rank` can never\n   return 4 for it.** A wound bleeds; blood loss is what bleeding produces.\n2. **`lifeThreatening` is a STAGE flag and starts at severity 0.60.**\n   `Data/Core/Defs/HediffDefs/Hediffs_Global_Misc.xml`, `BloodLoss`: five\n   stages, and only the fifth (`minSeverity 0.60`, \"extreme\") carries\n   `\u003clifeThreatening\u003etrue\u003c/lifeThreatening\u003e`. At 231,968 Captain's severity\n   back-solves to ~0.478 — the \"severe\" stage. **He was not even rank 3.** He\n   was rank 0, below `TendableNow` and below `Hediff_MissingPart`.\n3. Even granting the counterfactual, **rank 3 loses to twenty rank-4 rows\n   anyway.** There is no ordering over the existing four bands that surfaces\n   this row.\n\nSo the post-mortem's diagnosis stands as written, and the correction owed is to\nthe brief and not to it: the fix is NOT \"make the sort work\", the sort works.\n\n\nThe Scope's second option — \"a severity/lethality ordering that puts\nlife-threatening hediffs first\" — **would not have fixed this run**, because the\ngame's own `lifeThreatening` flag was false for the whole window that mattered.\nKeying on it reproduces the bug with a better-sounding rationale.\n\nThe band that generalises is **`HediffDef.lethalSeverity \u003e 0f`** — the game's own\nname for \"this hediff kills on its own clock when severity reaches it\"\n(`Verse/HediffDef.lethalSeverity`, default `-1f`; consumed at\n`Verse/Hediff.set_Severity` and `Verse/Hediff.CheckCauseDeath`, whose log line\nis literally `\"CauseOfDeath: lethal severity exceeded\"`). It is true for\n`BloodLoss` from severity 0.01, not from 0.60, and it picks up every disease and\ntoxin with a lethal ceiling — the same class, none of which bleed either. That\nis a new TOP band above bleeding, not a re-sort of the existing four: a wound\nthat is bleeding still outranks a tended flu.\n\nScope NARROWED accordingly: no `BloodLoss` special case, and the existing four\nbands are not touched.\n\n\n`Verse/Hediff.Visible` returns `CurStage.becomeVisible` when `visible` is false,\nand `BloodLoss` stage 0 sets `\u003cbecomeVisible\u003efalse\u003c/becomeVisible\u003e`. So below\nseverity 0.15 the row is legitimately absent — the serializer's `Visible` filter\nis the player's own filter and stays. **This is the argument for the clock being\nindependent of the hediff list**: `ticks_until_bleedout` must be computable when\nthe row is invisible, which it is, since\n`HealthUtility.TicksUntilDeathDueToBloodLoss` reads `BleedRateTotal` and\n`GetFirstHediffOfDef` directly and never consults `Visible`.","files":null}]}